<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Augustus the Younger, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1579">1579</a>–<a href="/years/1666">1666</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Augustus II of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Augustus the Younger was Duke of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a> who ruled the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfenbuttel">Wolfenbüttel</a> from 1635 until his death in 1666. A scholar and passionate collector, he built up the ducal library at Wolfenbüttel, which by his death was among the largest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and is now the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzog-august-library">Herzog August Library</a>. He also restored the principality after the devastation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/augustus-the-younger-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg.jpg" alt="Augustus the Younger, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anselm van Hulle · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hulle_Augustus_of_Brunswick-L%C3%BCneburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
